  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Li salts are hydrated <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>eg</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>LiCl</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>, because lithium-ion has high hydration enthalpy.</p><p>Smaller the size of cation more is the polarising power.<br />Polarising power order:&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Rb</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi>Cs</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></p>",
